From 250f12113d047eb0497a2c00fc80027c66b3991c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Fri, 17 Jul 2026 04:19:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: report RX chain signal for all RX paths

status->chains was set from the antenna mask, which is derived from
the number of spatial streams, while the chain_signal array is filled
from all RCPI fields. On boards where the number of RX paths exceeds
the stream count, e.g. the 3T3R mt7916/mt7981 variant with 2 streams
on the 5 GHz band, the RSSI of the extra chains was never reported.

Derive the chain mask from the RX path chainmask instead, shifted by
the band index of the phy owning the frame. On single-adie mt7986 the
main phy is bound to band 1 but its default chainmask is stored
without the band shift, unlike the mask set by mt7915_set_antenna();
fall back to the raw mask when the band group is empty to cover both
stored forms.

Fixes: e57b7901469f ("mt76: add mac80211 driver for MT7915 PCIe-based chipsets")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
 mt7915/mac.c | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -437,7 +437,14 @@ mt7915_mac_fill_rx(struct mt7915_dev *de
 		if (v0 & MT_PRXV_HT_AD_CODE)
 			status->enc_flags |= RX_ENC_FLAG_LDPC;
 
-		status->chains = mphy->antenna_mask;
+		/* The single-adie mt7986 default chainmask is stored without
+		 * the band shift, unlike the set_antenna path; fall back to
+		 * the raw mask when the band group is empty
+		 */
+		status->chains = mphy->chainmask >>
+				 (mphy->band_idx * dev->chainshift);
+		if (!status->chains)
+			status->chains = mphy->chainmask;
 		status->chain_signal[0] = to_rssi(MT_PRXV_RCPI0, v1);
 		status->chain_signal[1] = to_rssi(MT_PRXV_RCPI1, v1);
 		status->chain_signal[2] = to_rssi(MT_PRXV_RCPI2, v1);
